\nL200: \nL201: ### product line\nL202: \nL203: Sol-Gel Precursors\nL204: \nL205: ### assay\nL206: \nL207: 99.99% trace metals basis\nL208: ### form\nL209: \nL210: solid\nL211: \nL212: ### reaction suitability\nL213: \nL214: core: lanthanum, reagent type: inorganic catalyst\nL215: \nL216: ### impurities\nL217: \nL218: ≤150.0 ppm Trace Rare Earth Analysis\nL219: \nL220: ### mp\nL221: \nL222: 65-68 °C\nL223: \nL224: ### application(s)\nL225: \nL226: electroplating\nL227: material synthesis precursor\nL228: \nL229: ### SMILES string\nL230: \nL231: [La+3].[H]O[H].[H]O[H].[H]O[H].[H]O[H].[H]O[H].[H]O[H].[O-][N+]([O-])=O.[O-][N+]([O-])=O.[O-][N+]([O-])=O\nL232: \nL233: ### InChI\nL234: \nL235: 1S/La.3NO3.6H2O/c;3*2-1(3)4;;;;;;/h;;;;6*1H2/q+3;3*-1;;;;;;\nL236: \nL237: ### InChI key\nL238: \nL239: GJKFIJKSBFYMQK-UHFFFAOYSA-N\nL240: \nL241: Description\nL242: ### General description\nL243: \nL244: Lanthanum(III) nitrate hexahydrate is a transition metal catalyst widely used in many organic transformations. It can be prepared from lanthanum(III) oxide by treatment with N_{2}O_{4} or nitric acid. It is easy to handle and stable due to the presence of coordinative NO^{3−} moieties. It also finds application in the field of nanomaterial synthesis.\nL245: ### Application\nL246: \nL247: Lanthanum(III) nitrate hexahydrate can be used as a starting material:\nL248:   * For the electrochemical synthesis of a LaMnO_{3} thin film coating on stainless steel substrates.\nL249:   * In the solvothermal process for formation of doped lanthanide oxysulfide, La_{2}O_{2}S, in order to advance possible applications of this material in phosphors, fluorescent display tubes or heat transfer measurement.\nL250:   * For the chemoselective catalytic deprotection of acetonides.\nL251:   * In the preparation of highly active and nearly neutral lanthanum(III)nitrate alkoxide catalyst.\nL252: ### Features and Benefits\nL253: \nL254:   * High stability\nL255:   * Low toxicity\nL256:   * Mild reaction condition\nL257:   * Chemoselectivity\nL258:   * Inexpensive\nL259: \nL260: * * *\nL261: \nL262: ## Compare Similar Items\nL263: \nL264: 【18†View Full Comparison】\nL265: \nL266: * * *\nL267: \nL268: Show Differences\nL269: \nL270: [Input]\nL271: \nL272: 1 of 1\nL273: ###### This Item\nL274:  | 203548  | 217190  | 237957\nL275: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL276: 【19†Sigma-Aldrich 331937 Lanthanum(III) nitrate hexahydrate】[Button: Quick View]  | 【20†Sigma-Aldrich 203548 Lanthanum(III) nitrate hexahydrate】[Button: Quick View]  | 【21†Sigma-Aldrich 217190 Gadolinium(III) nitrate hexahydrate】[Button: Quick View]  | 【22†Sigma-Aldrich 237957 Yttrium(III) nitrate hexahydrate】[Button: Quick View]\nL277: description 99.99% trace metals basis  | description 99.999% trace metals basis  | description crystals and lumps, 99.999% trace metals basis  | description 99.8% trace metals basis\nL278: form solid  | form solid  | form crystals and lumps  | form crystals and lumps\nL279: assay 99.99% trace metals basis  | assay 99.999% trace metals basis  | assay 99.999% trace metals basis  | assay 99.8% trace metals basis\nL280: Quality Level 100  | Quality Level 200  | Quality Level 200  | Quality Level 200\nL281: mp 65-68 °C  | mp 65-68 °C  | mp 91 °C (lit.)  | mp-\nL282: impurities≤150.0 ppm Trace Rare Earth Analysis  | impurities≤15.0 ppm Trace Rare Earth Analysis  | impurities≤20.0 ppm Trace Rare Earth Analysis  | impurities≤2500.0 ppm Trace Rare Earth Analysis\nL283: product line Sol-Gel Precursors  | product line Sol-Gel Precursors  | product line-  | product line Sol-Gel Precursors\nL284: * * *\nL285: ### Still not finding the right product?\nL286: \nL287: Explore all of our products under 【23†Lanthanum(III) nitrate hexahydrate】\nL288: \nL289: 【23†View All Products】\nL290: \nL291: * * *\nL292: \nL293: ## Safety Information\nL294: \nL295: ### Pictograms\nL296: \nL297: 【24†GHS03,GHS05,GHS09】\nL298: \nL299: ### Signal Word\nL300: \nL301: Danger\nL302: \nL303: ### Hazard Codes\nL304: \nL305: 【25